      "confidence": 0.9,
      "curator_note": "gamma-H hydrogen rearrangement (McLafferty) of the carbonyl-n-ionized ester molecular ion through a 6-membered TS: the gamma H (H8, on C2) is transferred to the carbonyl oxygen O6, leaving a radical on the gamma carbon C2 and converting the ionized carbonyl into a protonated-carbonyl oxocarbenium (=O6(H8)+). Book draws 3 arcs; moves <1,2,3> are all drawn: <1> the O6 radical hook forming O6-H8, <2> the C2-H8 -> O6-H8 hook, <3> the C2-H8 homolysis hook leaving the radical on C2. Complete radical-site HAT, no implicit hooks."
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "evidence_step_alpha",
      "source_id": "mclafferty_ims_4e",
      "target_type": "step",
      "target_id": "step_alpha_cleavage",
      "support_type": "textbook_proposed",
      "locator": {
        "page": 82,
        "equation": "4.45",
        "figure": null,
        "panel": "alpha arrow to top-right products",
        "section": "4 / Basic Mechanisms of Ion Fragmentation"
      },
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "curator_note": "alpha-cleavage of the distonic ion: the gamma radical (C2) forms the C2=C3 pi bond while the beta C3-O4 bond cleaves, expelling neutral propene (R-CH=CH2) and leaving the ionized acid enol (acetic-acid radical cation, charge on O6 oxocarbenium, odd electron on the former ester O4). Book draws 0 arcs (the step is only labelled 'alpha'); all three moves <1,2,3> are implicit homolysis/pi-forming hooks required for electron balance (not drawn on the page). Resonance note: the book's top-right 4.45 product draws the complementary resonance form of this odd-electron acid ion -- H on the single-bonded oxygen (HO+) and the charge/odd electron on the double-bonded oxygen (+.O=); this record instead carries, consistently from the drawn intermediate, the oxocarbenium form (=O6(+)(H8) double-bonded, H on O6) with the odd electron localized on the former ester oxygen O4. The two are the same ionized acetic acid (C2H4O2+., m/z 60.02)."
    },
    {
