      "confidence": 0.6,
      "curator_note": "Cross-linked MOD rules (rule_index by_equation 4.45): IMS_4_45_rH and IMS_4_45_alpha. IMS_4_45_rH DFS [C]1[C]2([H]3)[C]4[O]5[C]6([C]7){=}[O+.]8>>[C]1[C.]2[C]4[O]5[C]6([C]7){=}[O+]8[H]3 matches step_rH exactly (gamma-H to carbonyl O, radical to gamma C, carbonyl O becomes oxocarbenium). MISMATCH on IMS_4_45_alpha: its DFS product [C]1[C]2[C]3.[O+.]4{=}[C]5([C]6)[O+]7[H]8 leaves the neutral C1-C2-C3 fragment fully saturated (no C2=C3 alkene pi bond is drawn, so it encodes a propane skeleton rather than propene) and carries TWO formal positive charges (O4+ and O7+) on the acid fragment, i.e. product charge +2 vs reactant +1 -- not charge-balanced. The cleaved bond (C3-O4) is correct and is incident to the pi-forming carbon C3, but the pi bond and charge count are mis-encoded."
